<title>USA: Tenn. housing term bonds free to trade at 0915 EDT.</title>
<headline>Tenn. housing term bonds free to trade at 0915 EDT.</headline>
<text>
<p>TENNESSEE HOUSING DEVELOPMENT AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $55,000,000</p>
<p>HOMEOWNERSHIP PROGRAM BONDS</p>
<p>ISSUE 1996-4A (AMT) &amp; ISSUE 1996-4B (NON-AMT)</p>
<p>Effective at 9:15 A.M. E.D.T., Thursday, September 5, 1996 all syndicate terms and price restrictions are removed on the term bonds ONLY, and the bonds will be free to trade.</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>First Tennessee Bank Memphis</p>
<p>Equitable Securities Corp.</p>
<p>Harris Trust and Savings Bank</p>
<p>Everen Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>George K. Baum &amp; Company</p>
<p>IN ASSOCIATION WITH:</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
